# How much of the world's seafood is farmed?
subtitle: "Draw how fish farming grew after 1990 beside the wild catch, then see why it took over: the sea's catch hit a ceiling decades ago."
tags: ["food","earth","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Caught or farmed?\" note \"1960: 6%\""

## How much of the world's seafood is farmed?
use: line_chart
with:
    x:
      - 1960
      - 1970
      - 1980
      - 1990
      - 2000
      - 2010
      - 2013
      - 2020
      - 2024
    series:
      - {name: Farmed, values: [[2.1, 3.7, 7.7, 17, null, null, null, null, null], [2.1, 3.7, 7.7, 17, 43.1, 78.1, 95, 122.8, 141.4]]}
      - {name: Wild catch, values: [[32.1, 56.8, 58.8, 76.4, 96.2, 89.7, 93.1, 91.6, 94.4], [32.1, 56.8, 58.8, 76.4, 96.2, 89.7, 93.1, 91.6, 94.4]]}
    stage: 0
    xlim:
      - 1960
      - 2032
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 160
    y_label: million tonnes
    points: true
    label_size: 28
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: 'Seafood production: wild fish catch vs. aquaculture'
      authors: Our World in Data, from FAO via World Bank (2026)
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/capture-fisheries-vs-aquaculture
      finding: aquaculture (fish, molluscs, crustaceans and aquatic plants) 2.1 Mt in 1960, 17 Mt in 1990, 95 Mt in 2013, 141 Mt in 2024; wild catch 32 Mt in 1960 and about 90–96 Mt every year since the mid-1990s (94 Mt in 2024); farming passed the wild catch in 2013; farmed share 60% in 2024 counting seaweed
    - id: sofia
      title: The State of World Fisheries and Aquaculture 2024
      authors: Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations
      year: 2024
      finding: in 2022 aquaculture produced 51% of aquatic animals (fish, shellfish), overtaking capture fisheries for the first time

    card title "How much seafood is farmed?"

How much of the world's seafood is farmed, rather than caught in the wild? The blue line is the wild catch, in million tonnes a year.
    draw axes line_2

Red is farmed: fish, shellfish and seaweed. In 1990, farms made seventeen million tonnes, a fifth as much as the wild catch.
    draw line_1

    ask "Draw the farmed line on to 2024." on line_1 from 2000 store g default 20,24,25,27,29
        right: Close. You saw the farms coming.
        wrong: Not quite. Farms grew far faster.

    animate stage 1 duration 1.5

In 2013 the farms passed the wild catch, and by 2024 they made about a hundred and forty million tonnes.
    dot cross #3d3833 at.data [2013,95]
    text cross_l "2013: farms overtake" #3d3833 at.data [1980,140] cites ["owid"] font_size 36

And look at the blue line: the wild catch has been stuck at around ninety million tonnes since the mid-1990s.
    path ceil dashed thick #2f6b8f points [[1993,104],[2024,104]] data true
    text ceil_l "ceiling ~90 Mt" #2f6b8f at.data [2000,114] cites ["owid"] font_size 38

The seas were fished to their limit, so all the growth since has come from farms.
    highlight line_1

    erase cross cross_l ceil ceil_l

That farmed total counts mussels, shrimp and seaweed too: sixty percent of everything.
    icon oyster size 120 set twemoji x 230 y 560 icon_look picture of oyster
    icon shrimp size 120 set twemoji x 370 y 560 icon_look picture of shrimp
    text incl "+ shellfish, seaweed" #8f887c x 300 y 465 font_size 36

    erase incl

Counting animals alone, farms passed the half-way mark in 2022.
    text half "animals only: ~half" #b5482e cites ["sofia"] x 300 y 465 font_size 36

    erase oyster shrimp half

So the picture of seafood as a boat hauling in a net is out of date: most of it now grows up in a farm.
    icon pole size 150 set twemoji x 290 y 540 icon_look picture of "fishing pole"

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon fish size 280 set twemoji x 540 y 420 icon_look picture of fish hidden true
    thumb s1 "WILD?" kind stamp x 640 y 650 angle -6 hidden true
    thumb s2 "FARMED?" kind stamp x 580 y 210 angle -8 hidden true
    thumb t1 "Where did your fish grow up?" kind question hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    text y1 "1960" #8f887c x 250 y 620 font_size 56 hidden true
    text n1 "6% farmed" #8f887c x 250 y 520 font_size 64 hidden true
    text y2 "today" #b5482e x 720 y 620 font_size 56 hidden true
    text n2 "?" #b5482e x 720 y 470 font_size 200 hidden true
    icon f size 170 set twemoji x 250 y 350 icon_look picture of "tropical fish" hidden true
    thumb t2 "Wild fish are out of date" kind band hidden true

## Thumbnail
role: thumbnail

    icon boat size 240 set twemoji x 270 y 470 icon_look picture of "fishing pole" hidden true
    text flat "wild catch: flat" #2f6b8f x 680 y 530 font_size 64 hidden true
    text so "since the 1990s" #b5482e x 680 y 400 font_size 60 hidden true
    thumb t3 "The sea hit a ceiling" kind band hidden true
